# a field is a definition declared outside the schema, at the top of the file: the file is the lineage, so what it declares beside the
# schemas is declared in the lineage outside the schema (rule ref-lineage-meta).
# Was testdata/lineage: schema contains a reference to an external type of struct kind
#issue: 21
-- in.cue --
import "github.com/sdboyer/thema"

thema.Lineage
name: "refexstruct"
schemas: {
	"0": "0": {
		schema: {
			aBaz: #Baz
		}
	}
}
lenses: {}

#Baz: {
    run:  string
    tell: bytes
    dat:  int32
}
-- out/bindfail --
schema 0.0: aBaz refers to #Baz, which is declared in the lineage outside the schema; a schema may refer only to its own body and CUE's builtin packages (rule ref-lineage-meta):
    ./in.cue:8:10
